  "body": {
    "id": "lem:conditional-calibration-concentration",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "Under \\(\\mathrm{ass:empirical-moment-perturbation}\\), conditionally on every construction sigma-field \\(\\mathcal D_{A,k}\\),\n\\[\n \\|\\widehat G_k^C-E[\\widehat D_{J_n}^{(-k,A)}\\widehat D_{J_n}^{(-k,A)\\top}\\mid\\mathcal D_{A,k}]\\|_{\\mathrm{op}}=O_p(\\eta_{G,n}),\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n \\|\\widehat c_k^C-E[\\widehat D_{J_n}^{(-k,A)}\\widehat B^{(-k,A)}\\mid\\mathcal D_{A,k}]\\|_2=O_p(\\eta_{c,n}),\n\\]\nuniformly over the fixed number of folds.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "k",
      "Traink",
      "Calibk",
      "Dn",
      "Ehat",
      "etaGram",
      "etaCross",
      "Kfold"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:empirical-moment-perturbation",
      "def:affine-ensemble-estimator",
      "def:inference-gauges"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Fix a fold and condition on \\(\\mathcal D_{A,k}\\); then the learned functions are fixed and the observations indexed by \\(\\mathcal C_k\\) are independent.  The assumed moment-generating-function inequality and exponential Markov inequality give, for every unit \\(u\\) and every \\(x>0\\),\n\\[\n \\Pr\\!\\left(\\left|n_{C,k}^{-1}\\sum_{i\\in\\mathcal C_k}X_{i,u}\\right|>x\\ \\middle|\\ \\mathcal D_{A,k}\\right)\n \\le 2\\exp\\!\\left[-c_1n_{C,k}\\min\\!\\left\\{\\frac{x^2}{B_{D,n}^4},\\frac{x}{B_{D,n}^2}\\right\\}\\right].\n\\]\nTo see this, apply Markov's inequality to the exponential of the sum, multiply the conditional moment-generating-function bounds by independence, optimize \\(\\lambda\\) over the permitted interval, and repeat with \\(-\\lambda\\).  A maximal \\(1/4\\)-separated subset of the Euclidean unit sphere has at most \\(9^{J_n}\\) elements by comparing the volumes of disjoint radius-\\(1/8\\) balls with a radius-\\(9/8\\) ball.  For a symmetric matrix \\(M\\), approximation of a maximizing unit vector by this net gives \\(\\|M\\|_{\\mathrm{op}}\\le2\\max_u|u^\\top Mu|\\).  A union bound over the net, followed by the preceding tail inequality, proves the Gram rate; the displayed \\(\\log(1+J_n)\\) factor is conservative relative to the net bound.\n\nThe same Chernoff calculation applied to \\(Z_{i,u}\\) gives\n\\[\n \\Pr\\!\\left(\\left|u^\\top(\\widehat c_k^C-E[\\widehat D\\widehat B\\mid\\mathcal D_{A,k}])\\right|>x\\ \\middle|\\ \\mathcal D_{A,k}\\right)\n \\le2\\exp\\!\\left[-c_2n_{C,k}\\min\\!\\left\\{\\frac{x^2}{B_{D,n}^2B_{0,n}^2},\\frac{x}{B_{D,n}B_{0,n}}\\right\\}\\right].\n\\]\nThe same net and the identity \\(\\|v\\|_2=\\sup_{\\|u\\|=1}|u^\\top v|\\) yield the cross-moment rate.  Since \\(K_{\\mathrm{fold}}\\) is fixed, a final finite union bound makes both conclusions uniform in \\(k\\).",
